  "description": "Create, edit, compress, sign and validate PDF files in .NET. Pure C#, MIT licensed, no native binaries and no Ghostscript. Lossless compression (object streams, compressed xref streams, deduplication, font merging, Flate recompression, lossless JPEG re-encoding) with an equivalence proof on every output, plus opt-in lossy image profiles. Merge, split and reorder pages; text extraction with reading order and right to left scripts; forms, annotations and flattening; PAdES signatures with timestamps and long term validation; PDF/A-1b to PDF/A-4 and Factur-X/ZUGFeRD; JPEG, JPEG 2000, JBIG2, CCITT, TIFF, PNG, GIF, BMP and WebP images; AES-256 encryption. Opens and saves large files with bounded memory and runs in containers, AWS Lambda and Azure Functions. No dependencies on .NET 8 and later; .NET Standard 2.0 for .NET Framework 4.6.2+. Native AOT compatible. By Jamal Abdelkhalek, JADEV.",
